    51→        title: Shadow Directory Structure
    52→        type: requirement
    53→        status:
    54→          maturity: draft
    55→          implementation: implemented
    56→        description: |
    57→          Directory layout for shadow branch:
    58→
    59→          project/
    60→            .kspec/                    # Git worktree (gitignored by main)
    61→              .git -> ../.git/worktrees/.kspec
    62→              kynetic.yaml             # Root manifest
    63→              kynetic.tasks.yaml       # Tasks
    64→              kynetic.meta.yaml        # Meta-spec
    65→              project.tasks.yaml       # Project tasks
    66→              project.inbox.yaml       # Inbox
    67→              modules/
    68→                core.yaml
    69→                cli.yaml
    70→                shadow.yaml
    71→            src/                       # Normal source (on main branch)
    72→            tests/
    73→            .gitignore                 # Contains: .kspec/
    74→
    75→          Shadow branch contents (at root):
    76→          - kynetic.yaml - manifest
    77→          - *.tasks.yaml - task files
    78→          - *.inbox.yaml - inbox files
    79→          - modules/*.yaml - spec modules
    80→        implements:
    81→          - '@shadow-concept'
    82→      - _ulid: 01KF1V1ZTYSNNVT5WP56VCP5YB
    83→        slugs:
    84→          - shadow-autocommit
    85→        title: Auto-Commit on State Changes
    86→        type: requirement
    87→        status:
    88→          maturity: draft
    89→          implementation: implemented
    90→        description: |-
    91→          All state-changing kspec commands automatically commit to shadow branch.
    92→
    93→          Commit messages by command:
    94→
    95→          Task lifecycle:
    96→          - task start @ref      -> "Start @{slug}"
    97→          - task complete @ref   -> "Complete @{slug}: {reason}"
    98→          - task block @ref      -> "Block @{slug}"
    99→          - task unblock @ref    -> "Unblock @{slug}"
   100→          - task cancel @ref     -> "Cancel @{slug}"
   101→          - task set @ref        -> "Update @{slug}"
   102→
   103→          Task notes/todos:
   104→          - task note @ref       -> "Note on @{slug}"
   105→          - task add             -> "Add task: {title}"
   106→          - task todo add        -> "Todo on @{slug}"
   107→          - task todo done       -> "Todo done on @{slug}"
   108→          - task todo undone     -> "Todo undone on @{slug}"
   109→
   110→          Inbox:
   111→          - inbox add            -> "Inbox: {text}"
   112→          - inbox promote        -> "Promote to @{slug}"
   113→          - inbox delete         -> "Inbox delete"
   114→
   115→          Items:
   116→          - item add/set/delete  -> "{action} @{slug}"
   117→          - item ac add          -> "AC on @{slug}"
   118→          - item ac set          -> "AC update on @{slug}"
   119→          - item ac remove       -> "AC remove on @{slug}"
   120→
   121→          Derive:
   122→          - derive               -> "Derive from @{spec}"
   123→
   124→          Implementation:
   125→          - After write, run: git -C .kspec add -A && git -C .kspec commit -m "..."
   126→          - Low overhead (local commits only)
   127→          - Commit includes all changes from the operation
   128→        implements:
   129→          - '@shadow-concept'
   130→        acceptance_criteria:
   131→          - id: ac-1
   132→            given: shadow branch is enabled and task @my-task exists
   133→            when: kspec task start/complete/block/unblock/cancel/set runs
   134→            then: shadow branch has new commit with appropriate message
   135→          - id: ac-2
   136→            given: shadow branch is enabled and task @my-task exists
   137→            when: kspec task note/add or task todo add/done/undone runs
   138→            then: shadow branch has new commit with appropriate message
   139→          - id: ac-3
   140→            given: shadow branch is enabled
   141→            when: kspec inbox add/promote/delete runs
   142→            then: shadow branch has new commit with appropriate message
   143→          - id: ac-4
   144→            given: shadow branch is enabled
   145→            when: kspec item add/set/delete or item ac add/set/remove runs
   146→            then: shadow branch has new commit with appropriate message
   147→          - id: ac-5
   148→            given: shadow branch is enabled and spec item @my-spec exists
   149→            when: kspec derive @my-spec runs
   150→            then: shadow branch has new commit with message containing the spec ref
   151→          - id: ac-6
   152→            given: shadow branch is enabled but commit fails (e.g., git error)
   153→            when: any state-changing command runs
   154→            then: command still succeeds, commit failure is silently ignored
