   423→      - shadow-recovery
   424→    title: Shadow Recovery
   425→    type: feature
   426→    status:
   427→      maturity: draft
   428→      implementation: implemented
   429→    priority: high
   430→    tags:
   431→      - infrastructure
   432→      - reliability
   433→    description: |
   434→      Recovery mechanisms for shadow branch issues. Provides CLI commands for
   435→      diagnosing and repairing shadow branch problems.
   436→
   437→      Commands:
   438→      - `shadow status`: Check health of shadow branch
   439→      - `shadow repair`: Recreate worktree when branch exists but worktree broken
   440→      - `shadow log`: View recent commits on shadow branch
   441→
   442→      Handles common issues:
   443→      - Worktree directory deleted (recreate from existing branch)
   444→      - Worktree disconnected from git (remove and recreate)
   445→      - Stale worktree references in git
   446→    acceptance_criteria:
   447→      - id: ac-recovery-1
   448→        given: shadow branch exists but .kspec/ directory is deleted
   449→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   450→        then: worktree is recreated from existing branch
   451→      - id: ac-recovery-2
   452→        given: .kspec/ exists but .git file is missing or corrupt
   453→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   454→        then: worktree is removed and recreated
   455→      - id: ac-recovery-3
   456→        given: shadow branch does not exist
   457→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   458→        then: it fails with error suggesting kspec init
   459→      - id: ac-recovery-4
   460→        given: shadow branch is healthy
   461→        when: kspec shadow repair runs
   462→        then: it succeeds without changes (idempotent)
   463→      - id: ac-recovery-5
   464→        given: shadow branch is healthy
   465→        when: kspec shadow status runs
   466→        then: it reports healthy status with all checks passing
   467→      - id: ac-recovery-6
   468→        given: shadow branch has issues
   469→        when: kspec shadow status runs
   470→        then: it reports the specific issue and suggests repair
   471→    requirements:
